.SH DESCRIPTION
Tears down the debugger for the current session.
Performs the following actions:
.IP "1." 3
If the pre\-command hook is registered, unregisters it via
\f[CR]unregister_pre_command_hook()\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
Walks the breakpoint linked list, freeing each breakpoint\(cqs
\f[CR]pattern\f[R], \f[CR]condition\f[R], and the breakpoint node
itself.
.IP "3." 3
Resets \f[CR]active\f[R] to 0 and \f[CR]pending_cmd\f[R] to NULL.
.PP
This function is called when the client sends a \f[CR]disable\f[R] debug
message, or during session teardown.
.SH PARAMETERS
None.
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
